        600k Super Randonnee:    https://ridewithgps.com/routes/48559725\\nhttps://rusa.org/cgi-bin/permview_GF.pl?permid=5150\\nTime
        Limit: 60 hours\\nA Super Randonee from NYC\u2019s Front door!  \\nRoute Description:\\nThis
        route will start on Henry Hudson Drive (River Road) ROAD IS CURRENTLY CLOSED
        AT GREAT WALL REROUTE ONTO 9w for first 8 miles! as it winds North away from
        the city.  Traveling to the apple orchards, and up to Bear Mountain NY.  The
        route will then continue up Mine road and onto the storm king highway, eventually
        making its way down to Wawayanda and then up and over to the High Point Monument,
        which is the highest point in NJ!  Then quickly dropping down into Pennsylvania
        and meandering through the Delaware river watershed till reaching Lake Wallenpaupack
        (the second largest lake in PA). The route will then work its way down through
        the Delaware State forest and cross the Delaware for a third time! going back
        into NJ and the Delaware Water Gap Recreational area.  Once exiting the Delaware
        water gap the route will travel through the hills and lakes of Morris and
        Passaic Counties before returning to the George Washington Bridge.\\n\\nThere
        will be an abundance of food options as well as lodging throughout the course,
        becoming more scarce as you travel west and then ramping back up as you travel
        back east.  The options listed on the RWGPS are just a small selection of
        what is available, there are many gems to be discovered!\\n\\n\\nROAD ACCESS:\\nMile
        0 Henry Hudson Drive: ROAD IS CURRENTLY CLOSED AT GREAT WALL REROUTE ONTO
        9w for first 8 miles!\\nOpen 6am till 9pm Daily.\\nMile 54.8 MINE ROAD:\\nMust
        check Westpoint website to check if road has a scheduled closure \\nhttps://westpoint.isportsman.net/Areas.aspx\\nMile
        47.1 BEAR MOUNTAIN PERKINS DRIVE:  \\nApril 1 - November 30, weather permitting.
        Dawn till Dusk\\nMile 65.5 Storm King Highway Frequent closures due to weather
        or maintenance.\\nUse Route 9W alternative if closed.\\nMile 132.2 HIGH POINT
        SCENIC DRIVE: Scenic Drive is open 8am-8pm\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCAUTIONS:\\n@mile
        213.5\\nBeaver Dam Road is Gravel,  watch out for loose grave/rocks/ruts\\n@mile
        233.3\\nFive Mile Meadow Road : Watch out for ruts, roots, and loose gravel.
        \\nYou may detour by continuing on Dingman Ferry Turnpike if you wish to avoid.\\n@mile
